Thu Nov 19 08:55:18 UTC 2026 - Michael Pujos <pujos.michael@gmail.com>

- Update to 1.0.0
  * Highlights
    - Multithreaded rendering: r_threads is on by default as Auto (-1),
      which picks and tunes the worker count itself. 0 turns it off.
      It's also in the Performance menu. At 1080p it gave about 1.5–3x
      the FPS, and less on heavy maps. timedemo_threads benchmarks each
      worker count
    - Much faster on big maps: the edge and span code was rewritten,
      edge caching fixed, and coarse occlusion and BSP culling improved.
      Brush entities are now culled too (r_entocclusion and r_bmodelocclusion,
      both Auto). That's up to 50% more fps on heavy maps
    - Faster at high resolutions: with SDL 3.4+ on a GPU renderer, the palette
      lookup runs on the GPU (1440p went from 87 to 129 fps in testing)
    - Interpolation, ported from Mark V: model animation (r_lerpmodels),
      movement (r_lerpmove), light styles (r_lerplightstyles) and
      sky (r_skysmooth), with an exclusion list in r_nolerp_list.
      There's a new Interpolation menu, and v_gunkick 2 gives smooth recoil.
      All of it is off by default and on in the Fancy preset.
    - New fog: it now follows Ironwail's curve and fades, and is dithered
      toward the exact fog colour (r_fogdither)
    - Huge maps load without -heapsize (Immortal and others), because memory
      now grows as needed. The max_edicts default went up to 16384 and static
      entities to 4096
    - Quake 64 map support
  * Rendering
    - The z-buffer is now 32-bit, so distant models no longer show through walls.
      Entities pressed against walls or water no longer poke through either
    - The picture matches the original WinQuake more closely: spans, rounding,
      model clipping and lighting, and sky projection
    - Several translucent layers can now overlap
    * Skyboxes:
      - PNG files and any size now load
      - They're dithered more smoothly
      - A map can use any number of skies
      - Sky names are case-insensitive
      - Sky on brush entities draws correctly
    - The scale entity field now works on models and sprites
    * Map fixes:
      -  Missing floors and walls around ericw fence brushes are drawn again,
         along with areas vis had hidden
      -  Doors set in solid no longer vanish
      -  Huge brush models and coordinates draw correctly
      -  Lit and black liquids are fixed
    * Textures:
      -  Broken or all-black mipmaps are rebuilt (r_rebuildmips)
      -  New r_cutoutmipscale cvar
      -  Fullbright pixels stay on distant models
      -  Coloured lighting no longer makes holes in models
    - The picture is sharp on scaled (HiDPI) Wayland and macOS displays
    - The Modern FOV mode (r_fovmode 1) now widens the view on widescreens like
      QuakeSpasm and Ironwail. fov now means the horizontal FOV at 4:3
  * Mods and gameplay
    - New sv_gameplayfix_elevators and sv_gameplayfix_random, from Ironwail
    - You can no longer look around during camera cutscenes
    - The weapon is kept through resurrect
    - mg1's fog triggers work
    - Screen tints reset on disconnect (AD's books)
    - The game command now properly resets the palette, sounds, CSQC and demo list
    - File names are case-insensitive, and Windows-style paths in mods work
    - Saves with braces in strings load
    - Corrupt models are tolerated (the vore in The Purifier)
    - Fixed the "PR_GetString: invalid string offset" error in some mods
    - Skin colour 255 is cut out only on models flagged as holey
  * Console and UI
    - New commands: apropos/find, condump, bindlist, setpos, viewpos, and ban
    * New cvars:
      - r_flatlightstyles: steady lights, for players bothered by flicker
      - scr_showspeed: shows your speed
      - snd_allowpause: pauses world sounds with the game (off by default)
    - Typing a cvar name on its own now shows its default value
    - New menu pages: Sound (under New Options), Interpolation, and Multithreading
  * Sound
    - Ambient sounds work above 100 fps
    - No loud second of music at startup
    - sndspeed is now saved
  * Stability
     Many crashes and undefined-behaviour bugs were fixed:
      - malformed maps, models, textures, WAVs, TGAs and gfx.wad files
      - very long names
      - demos inside paks
      - misaligned data, which crashed ARM builds
  * Platforms and build
    - New MinGW toolchain files for Windows XP (32-bit) and 64-bit Windows
    - MSVC, Android, ARM, and RISC-V fixes
  * Removed cvars
    - Replaced by the new fog: r_fogstyle, r_fognoise, r_fogfactor, r_fogscale
    - Unused: r_timegraph, r_graphheight, r_dspeeds, r_polymodelstats, screensize,
      external_textures, snd_mixspeed, snd_noextraupdate

